.github.com/users/lauwers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lauwers/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-31T16:32:16Z","updated_at":"2021-03-31T16:32:16Z","body":"I tried that, but that seems like a very inconvenient workaround. In some of my classes I have a dozen of these containment relationships. I shouldn’t have to go patch up my code in dozens and dozens of places to fix something that isn’t a problem in the first place. Can you please provide an option to suppress these warnings without having to annotate the relationship definitions themselves?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nChris\r\n\r\nFrom: mike bayer ***@***.***>\r\nSent: Wednesday, March 31, 2021 9:18 AM\r\nTo: sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy ***@***.***>\r\nCc: Chris Lauwers ***@***.***>; Author ***@***.***>\r\nSubject: Re: [sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy] Incorrect \"conflicting relationship\" warning message (#6171)\r\n\r\n\r\nhi there -\r\n\r\nthis is from #5171<https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/5171> and the warning includes the action to take for this special case:\r\n\r\nThe 'overlaps' parameter may be used to remove this warning.\r\n\r\nthe warnings are resolved if you use this:\r\n\r\nclass Container(Base):\r\n\r\n    __tablename__ = 'containers'\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n\r\n    name = Column(String)\r\n\r\n    boxes = relationship(\"Box\", backref=\"container\", overlaps=\"container\")\r\n\r\n    bags = relationship(\"Bag\", backref=\"container\", overlaps=\"container\")\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, name):\r\n\r\n        self.name = name\r\n\r\nthe docs are not great here and we could use an errors.rst entry\r\n\r\n—\r\nYou are receiving this because you authored the thread.\r\nReply to this email directly, view it on GitHub<https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6171#issuecomment-811195369>, or unsubscribe<https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/A